Update Coefficients Of Univariate Linear Regression.At each iteration (epoch), the values of the regression coefficient are updated by a specific value wrt to the error from the previous iteration. This updation is very crucial and is the crux of the machine learning applications that you write. Updating the coefficients is done by penalizing their value with a fraction of the error that its previous values caused. This fraction is called the learning rate. This defines how fast our model reaches to point of convergence(the point where the error is ideally 0). b_i = b_i - \alpha * \left( \frac{\partial}{\partial b} cost(x, y) \right)             
